# Git: no commits or pushes

The repository owner commits and pushes all changes herself.

- Never run `git commit`, `git push`, `git push --force`, `git tag`, or anything that rewrites or publishes history
  (including `git merge`, `git rebase`, `git reset` on shared branches).
- Do not change remotes (`git remote set-url/add/remove`).
- Read-only git commands are fine: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, `git show`, `git fetch`.
- After editing files, finish with a short list of the changed files so the user can review and push.

```bash
# ❌ Don't
git add . && git commit -m "fix" && git push

# ✅ Do
git status --short   # then report the changed files to the user
```
